    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d425">

                <pb facs="0442" n="352" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg352"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/10309</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the British Chargé</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hohler</hi>)</head>
                <p>The Secretary of State presents his compliments to the Chargé d’ Affaires <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ad interim</hi> of Great Britain, and has the honor to
                    acknowledge the receipt of the British Embassy’s memorandum of June 10, 1918,
                    respecting the question of the transportation to France of Czecho-Slovak troops
                    now in Russian territory.</p>
                <p>In reply the Secretary of State begs to inform the British Chargé d’Affaires that
                    the delay in acknowledging the Embassy’s memorandum was unavoidable on account
                    of the uncertainty of the Siberian situation and that the Department of State
                    will reserve judgment in the matter until the situation has become more
                    clarified.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-08-21"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">August 21, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
